[sliver] Functional spring-root clearance roof: this full-Y 0.85 mm face ends the open lane between the rigid cap and each spring wing at Z4.2. The lane leaves 6.7 mm from root to hook bearing for outward insertion flex. Filling it joins the wing to the rigid half at Z1.15, reducing that length to 3.65 mm and raising the simple cantilever strain estimate at 0.6 mm deflection from 2.89% to 9.73%. It is the boundary of the working spring lane, not a residual strip between independent cuts.
alternatives: Filling the lane defeats the selected flex length. Thickening the wing to 3 mm at the same length gives a 6.01% beam estimate; retaining 2.89% would need about 9.67 mm of spring length and a taller cap that enters V-B's inlet during the 6.65 mm vertical approach. These are geometric beam estimates, not an elastic solution or lifetime result.
