[sliver] Functional hook bearing face: its 0.70 mm radial span contains the 0.25 mm sliding side allowance and 0.45 mm positive capture under the receiver ledge. The integral hook is 3 mm tall including its lead-in nose; this narrow contact face does not define a thin fixed wall. The cap prints along Y, placing this entire hook section in every layer. The current emitted-path reading samples both hooks and records at least 99.15% bead coverage across the cap's sampled sections.
alternatives: Filling the inboard side removes the clearance that lets the hook pass the receiver. Removing the projection removes positive retention. Increasing the receiver projection to 3 mm widens the complete matching cap by 4.8 mm; the current native deflected-body probe then leaves only 0.299359 mm to J2-COM against the 1 mm wire-clearance requirement. The current full-span bearing preserves that required space.
