[thin] Intentional moving spring leaves: the 1.44 mm section supplies outward bending over the receiver while the rigid cap, receiver and axial shoulders retain their 3 mm fixed sections. This thickness follows the physically accepted display-wing section as a printability precedent, without transferring its retention acceptance to this cap. The current cap prints end-on along Y with three Classic loops and 100% infill, so the X/Z spring section and its bending lie in each layer. hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/reservoir-a-snap-review/print/review.json records actual emitted beads through both leaves, both hooks and the roof, with minimum sampled coverage 99.15% and no supports.
alternatives: A 3 mm leaf at the same 6.7 mm free length and 0.6 mm deflection raises the beam estimate from 2.89% to 6.01%. Keeping the lower estimate with 3 mm leaves requires approximately 9.67 mm free length; raising that root and roof obstructs V-B's inlet along the 6.65 mm approach. Shortening or filling the spring lane increases strain further. Printed insertion force, retention and repeated-use life remain unqualified.
